Subject: Allow host frames to finish without presentation

Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4

Provide an explicit non-presenting end operation for discarded/failed game
frames. Retain FIFO draining, resource submission, completion callbacks, ImGui
frame closure and staging-slot recovery, while skipping surface acquisition and
presentation. This finishes queued work; it is not a rollback of EFB writes.
Existing aurora_end_frame callers retain their behavior.

diff --git a/include/aurora/aurora.h b/include/aurora/aurora.h
--- a/include/aurora/aurora.h
+++ b/include/aurora/aurora.h
@@ -132,6 +132,9 @@
 const AuroraEvent* aurora_update();
 bool aurora_begin_frame();
 void aurora_end_frame();
+// Finish queued rendering and callbacks, but do not acquire/present a surface.
+// Pair with a successful aurora_begin_frame for discarded or failed host frames.
+void aurora_end_frame_no_present();
 
 void aurora_set_log_level(AuroraLogLevel level);
 void aurora_set_pause_on_focus_lost(bool value);
diff --git a/lib/aurora.cpp b/lib/aurora.cpp
--- a/lib/aurora.cpp
